{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{110}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the least-squares solution of $Ax=b$, where \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48fc2839-660f-57b5-b91c-b2fcd5bae103" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354439 #edb/ref 1074 "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{align