ref 17592186045417] [17592186500187 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500187 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "112e9326-3d57-5ecf-afb8-b6f921f35c4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140953" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b37b44d-e7cb-5e9e-b8af-e9f1e4941b43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500322 #edb/ref 1074 "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500387 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500387 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0c175108-3251-5f6f-a837-933e8a149a06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500387 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186326908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500391 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1daadfd6-2782-5d18-911b-b764bf042f15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500391 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500431 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500431 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a561b4d8-a24f-5ea9-9176-71cdc5599a2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500431 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186354410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500445 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 175921865